{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Abi89GknB6Ts"},"source":["# 🧰 Python Predefined Libraries & Methods: String & Date/Time Guide (Grade 8)\n","**Learning Objectives:**\n","1. Understand why we use **Predefined Libraries** (the Toolbox Analogy).\n","2. Clean and format messy user text using built-in **String Methods** (`strip()`, `title()`, `upper()`, `lower()`, `len()`, etc.).\n","3. Work with dates and schedules using the **`datetime` module** and `strftime()` format codes.\n","4. Integrate String Manipulation, Date/Time handling, Arrays/Lists, and Loops.\n","5. Complete practical activities: **Student Information Formatter**, **Deadline Formatter**, and the **Student Event Registration System** with GitHub versioning guidelines.\n","\n","---\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"GARWK0-KB6Ty"},"source":["## 🧰 Part 1: Predefined Libraries & String Manipulation\n","\n","A **Library** is like a toolbox. If a useful tool already exists, you don't need to build it from zero!\n","\n","### Common String Cleaning Tasks:\n","* `strip()`: Removes extra leading and trailing spaces.\n","* `title()`: Capitalizes the first letter of each word (proper name formatting).\n","* `upper()`: Converts all characters to UPPERCASE.\n","* `lower()`: Converts all characters to lowercase.\n","* `len()`: Counts total characters (including spaces).\n","* `find(substr)`: Locates the starting position of a substring.\n","* `isdigit()` / `isalpha()`: Checks if text consists strictly of numbers or letters.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"-u2u35E1B6Tz"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Run this cell to test Python String Cleaning Methods!\n","\n","messy_name = \"   juan dela cruz   \"\n","messy_section = \" magnesium \"\n","messy_subject = \"computer science\"\n","\n","# 1. Clean extra spaces & format proper title case\n","clean_name = messy_name.strip().title()\n","print(\"Cleaned Name:\", clean_name)\n","\n","# 2. Convert to Uppercase\n","name_code = clean_name.upper()\n","section_code = messy_section.strip().upper()\n","print(\"Name Code:\", name_code)\n","print(\"Section Code:\", section_code)\n","\n","# 3. Format Subject & Count Characters\n","clean_subject = messy_subject.strip().title()\n","char_count = len(clean_name)\n","\n","print(\"Formatted Subject:\", clean_subject)\n","print(\"Character Count of Name:\", char_count)\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"bJv1KL5EB6T1"},"source":["---\n","## 📝 Activity 1: Student Information Formatter\n","\n","**Task:** Create a program that asks for student details and displays formatted output according to PSHS standards.\n","\n","**Required Fields:**\n","1. First Name\n","2. Last Name\n","3. Section\n","4. Favorite Subject\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"66lSmZY5B6T1","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794897835299,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":15340,"user":{"displayName":"JURICH FAITH PASCUA","userId":"17042713211989153851"}},"outputId":"4586db97-cc00-4998-faee-e1a81c094a99"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Enter your first name:jurich\n","Enter your last name:pascua\n","Enter your section:acacia\n","Enter your favorite subject:chemistry\n","--- Formatted Output ---\n","Name: jurich pascua\n","Name Code: JURICH PASCUA\n","Section: acacia\n","Favorite Subject: chemistry\n","Character Count: 13\n"]}],"source":["# Activity 1 Implementation Code\n","# Test with messy inputs like '  juan ', ' dela cruz ', 'narra ',' acacia ', 'mahogany ', '  molave ' 'computer science'\n","\n","first_name = input(\"Enter your first name:\")\n","last_name = input(\"Enter your last name:\")\n","section = input(\"Enter your section:\")\n","fav_subject = input(\"Enter your favorite subject:\")\n","\n","# Cleaning and formatting logic\n","#### Add your Code here ####\n","full_name = first_name.strip() + \" \" + last_name.strip()\n","full_name_upper = full_name.strip().upper()\n","formatted_section = section.strip()\n","formatted_subject = fav_subject.strip()\n","char_count = len(full_name)\n","\n","print(\"--- Formatted Output ---\")\n","print(f\"Name: {full_name}\")\n","print(f\"Name Code: {full_name_upper}\")\n","print(f\"Section: {formatted_section}\")\n","print(f\"Favorite Subject: {formatted_subject}\")\n","print(f\"Character Count: {char_count}\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"v1v1jmGGB6T2"},"source":["---\n","## ⏰ Part 2: Predefined Libraries for Date & Time\n","\n","Dates are tricky because of leap years, month length differences, and different global formats. Python's `datetime` module makes handling schedules easy!\n","\n","### Key `strftime()` Formatting Codes:\n","* `%B` : Full month name (e.g., `June`)\n","* `%b` : Abbreviated month name (e.g., `Jun`)\n","* `%d` : Day of the month with zero-padding (e.g., `03`)\n","* `%Y` : 4-digit year (e.g., `2026`)\n","* `%A` : Full weekday name (e.g., `Wednesday`)\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"s0yNQC38B6T3","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794898078043,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":8,"user":{"displayName":"JURICH FAITH PASCUA","userId":"17042713211989153851"}},"outputId":"3a659802-3470-44b8-a200-b20547383ee1"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Formatted Date: June 03, 2026\n","Year: 2026\n","Month: June\n","Day: 3\n","Weekday: Wednesday\n"]}],"source":["from datetime import datetime\n","\n","# Creating a specific date object: datetime(year, month, day)\n","event_date = datetime(2026, 6, 3)\n","\n","# Formatting using strftime()\n","readable_date = event_date.strftime(\"%B %d, %Y\")\n","weekday_name = event_date.strftime(\"%A\")\n","month_name = event_date.strftime(\"%B\")\n","\n","print(\"Formatted Date:\", readable_date)\n","print(\"Year:\", event_date.year)\n","print(\"Month:\", month_name)\n","print(\"Day:\", event_date.day)\n","print(\"Weekday:\", weekday_name)\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"P1e35wADB6T4"},"source":["---\n","## 📅 Activity 2: Deadline & Date Formatter\n","\n","**Task:** Prompt the user for an event title, year, month, and day, then output a clean schedule card with the weekday!\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"G4PcRYRnB6T4","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794899173583,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":6448,"user":{"displayName":"JURICH FAITH PASCUA","userId":"17042713211989153851"}},"outputId":"f9cd686f-31de-4d0b-d8ed-4520f83fabbe"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Enter event title:hi\n","Enter the year of the event:2086\n","Enter the month of the event:5\n","Enter the day of the event:3\n","--- Formatted Output ---\n","Event: hi\n","Date: May 03, 2086\n","Year: 2086\n","Month: May\n","Day: 03\n","Weekday: Friday\n"]}],"source":["# Activity 2: Deadline & Date Formatter\n","# Input Data from user\n","from datetime import datetime\n","\n","event_title = input(\"Enter event title:\")\n","year = input(\"Enter the year of the event:\")\n","month = input(\"Enter the month of the event:\")\n","day = input(\"Enter the day of the event:\")\n","\n","# Create datetime object\n","event_date = datetime(int(year), int(month), int(day))\n","\n","readable_day = event_date.strftime(\"%d\")\n","weekday_name = event_date.strftime(\"%A\")\n","month_name = event_date.strftime(\"%B\")\n","formatted_date = event_date.strftime(\"%B %d, %Y\")\n","\n","\n","print(\"--- Formatted Output ---\")\n","print(f\"Event: {event_title}\")\n","print(f\"Date: {formatted_date}\")\n","print(f\"Year: {year}\")\n","print(f\"Month: {month_name}\")\n","print(f\"Day: {readable_day}\")\n","print(f\"Weekday: {weekday_name}\")\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dprG1q6nB6T5"},"source":["---\n","## 🔄 Part 3: Integrating Strings, Dates, Arrays & Loops\n","\n","Real-world applications often process lists of records. Below, we loop over an array of unformatted student registrations, cleaning the text and formatting the dates automatically.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"metadata":{"id":"ELXxlLEwB6T6","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1794948425427,"user_tz":-480,"elapsed":54,"user":{"displayName":"JURICH FAITH PASCUA","userId":"17042713211989153851"}},"outputId":"76e5a465-c1a7-4dd3-889c-fd85d1d3f6d6"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["=== AUTOMATED BATCH REGISTRATION FORMATTER ===\n","\n","--- Student 1 ---\n","Name: Juan Dela Cruz\n","Name Code: JUAN DELA CRUZ\n","Section: Molave\n","Event: Science Fair\n","Date: June 03, 2026 (Wednesday)\n","\n","--- Student 2 ---\n","Name: Maria Clara\n","Name Code: MARIA CLARA\n","Section: Acacia\n","Event: Robotics Competition\n","Date: November 15, 2026 (Sunday)\n","\n","--- Student 3 ---\n","Name: Pedro Penduko\n","Name Code: PEDRO PENDUKO\n","Section: Mahogany\n","Event: Hackathon\n","Date: February 20, 2027 (Saturday)\n"]}],"source":["\n","from datetime import datetime\n","\n","# Parallel arrays for student registration details\n","names = [\"  juan dela cruz \", \" maria clara \", \" pedro penduko \"]\n","sections = [\"molave \", \" acacia\", \"mahogany\"]\n","events = [\" science fair \", \" robotics competition \", \"hackathon \"]\n","\n","years = [2026, 2026, 2027]\n","months = [6, 11, 2]\n","days = [3, 15, 20]\n","\n","print(\"=== AUTOMATED BATCH REGISTRATION FORMATTER ===\")\n","\n","# Process each registration using the same index\n","for idx in range(len(names)):\n","    # Clean text\n","    clean_name = names[idx].strip().title()\n","    name_code = clean_name.upper()\n","    clean_section = sections[idx].strip().title()\n","    clean_event = events[idx].strip().title()\n","\n","    # Format date\n","    event_dt = datetime(years[idx], months[idx], days[idx])\n","    formatted_date = event_dt.strftime(\"%B %d, %Y (%A)\")\n","\n","    # Display formatted registration\n","    print(f\"\\n--- Student {idx+1} ---\")\n","    print(f\"Name: {clean_name}\")\n","    print(f\"Name Code: {name_code}\")\n","    print(f\"Section: {clean_section}\")\n","    print(f\"Event: {clean_event}\")\n","    print(f\"Date: {formatted_date}\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"KeK7u3U2B6T6"},"source":["---\n","## 🚀 Part 4: Independent Learning Activity-Student Event Registration System\n","\n","### Complete Application Implementation with GitHub Versioning\n","\n","Follow the study guide's versioning requirements:\n","* **Version 1:** Basic input and raw output.\n","* **Version 2:** Added string formatting (`strip()`, `title()`, `upper()`).\n","* **Version 3:** Added date/time formatting (`datetime`, `strftime()`).\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"OpQBGpn7B6T7"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Version 3 Implementation (Student Event Registration)\n","from datetime import datetime\n","\n","def run_event_registration():\n","    print(\"=== Student Event Registration ===\")\n","\n","    # 1. Inputs\n","    fname = input(\"Student First Name: \")\n","    lname = input(\"Student Last Name: \")\n","    sec = input(\"Section: \")\n","    evt = input(\"Event Name: \")\n","    yr = int(input(\"Event Year (YYYY): \"))\n","    mo = int(input(\"Event Month (1-12): \"))\n","    dy = int(input(\"Event Day (1-31): \"))\n","\n","    # 2. String Manipulation\n","    full_name = (fname.strip() + \" \" + lname.strip()).title()\n","    name_code = full_name.upper()\n","    clean_section = sec.strip().title()\n","    clean_event = evt.strip().title()\n","\n","    # 3. Date Handling\n","    event_dt = datetime(yr, mo, dy)\n","    formatted_date = event_dt.strftime(\"%B %d, %Y (%A)\")\n","\n","    # 4. Formatted Summary Output\n","    print(\"\" + \"=\" * 40)\n","    print(\"  Student Event Registration Summary\")\n","    print(\"=\" * 40)\n","    print(f\"Name: {full_name}\")\n","    print(f\"Name Code: {name_code}\")\n","    print(f\"Section: {clean_section}\")\n","    print(f\"Event: {clean_event}\")\n","    print(f\"Date: {formatted_date}\")\n","\n","# Run the function\n","run_event_registration()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"N62YCkBhB6T7"},"source":["---\n","## 📑 Part 5: README.md & Reflection Guide\n","\n","### 📌 README.md Template for GitHub Submission\n","```markdown\n","# Student Event Registration Formatter\n","\n","## Description\n","This program cleans user-submitted student details and formats event deadlines clearly using built-in Python string methods and the datetime module.\n","\n","## Language Used\n","Python 3\n","\n","## String Features Used\n","- `strip()`: removes extra spaces at the start and end of the input.\n","- `title()`: capitalizes the first letter of each word for clean names.\n","- `upper()`: converts the name to all capital letters for the Name Code.\n","\n","## Date/Time Features Used\n","- `datetime`: creates a real date object from the year, month, and day.\n","- `strftime()`: formats the date into a readable form like \"June 03, 2026 (Wednesday)\".\n","\n","## Version History\n","- Version 1: Initial version with basic input and raw output.\n","- Version 2: Added string formatting.\n","- Version 3: Integrated date/time formatting.\n","```\n","\n","---\n","### 💭 Reflection Starter Prompts\n","Complete these 5 sentences based on your work:\n","1. In my first version, my program could only accept basic input and show raw output.\n","2. I improved my program by adding string formatting and date/time formatting.\n","3. The string method I used was/were `strip()`, `title()`, and `upper()` because they clean up messy user input and make the names look proper and consistent.\n","4. The date/time feature I used was/were `datetime` and `strftime()` because they turn numbers into a real date and display it in a readable format with the weekday.\n","5. The biggest change in my program was combining string cleaning and date formatting into one complete registration system."]}],"metadata":{"language_info":{"name":"python"},"colab":{"provenance":[{"file_id":"1P47KDb-BR4awLpCmL2hOhfj1ymGw0qDF","timestamp":1794880014833}]},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}